+## ⛔ STOP — read this before editing ANY file or building
+
+This fork is a **child-theme overlay**. The upstream tree is kept **byte-for-byte
+pristine**; every NexaLance change lives in `nexa/`. Two rules, both learned the
+hard way on 2026-07-25:
+
+**1. NEVER edit a file outside `nexa/`.**
+Put the change in `nexa/patches/<path-with-__-instead-of-slashes>.patch`:
+```bash
+git diff upstream-main -- <file> > nexa/patches/<slug>.patch
+git checkout upstream-main -- <file>          # restore pristine
+node nexa/gen-manifest.mjs                    # register it
+node nexa/check/pristine-base.mjs             # must print ✓ pristine
+```
+If a patch for that file already exists, **merge into it** — do not overwrite:
+restore pristine → `git apply` the existing patch → re-add your change → re-cut.
+The pre-commit hook now enforces this. Do **not** bypass it with `--no-verify`.
+
+**2. NEVER build with plain `docker build` / `npm run build`.**
+The deploy build is:
+```bash
+node nexa/build.mjs        # apply patches → build → auto-restore
+```
+A plain `docker build` skips patch application, so the image silently loses every
+overlay customisation. This actually happened: an image built that way dropped all
+12 `gpt-5.6` models (222 → 204) because they come from
+`nexa/patches/open-sse__config__providers__registry__codex__index.ts.patch`, not
+from upstream source. It was caught only by diffing `/v1/models` before/after.
+
+**After ANY deploy, verify the model roster** — count + spot-check `gpt-5.6`:
+```bash
+curl -s -H "authorization: Bearer $OMNIROUTE_API_KEY" \
+  https://omni.nexaconnect.cloud/v1/models | python3 -c \
+  'import sys,json;i=[m["id"] for m in json.load(sys.stdin)["data"]];print(len(i),[x for x in i if "5.6" in x][:3])'
+```
+Healthy = **222 models** with `codex/gpt-5.6-*` present. A drop means patches did
+not apply — roll back and rebuild via `nexa/build.mjs`.
+
+Full rules: `nexa/README.md` (Golden rules) and the `nexa-overlay` skill in
+`.claude/skills/`.
